{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1395824-past-is-prologue-available-now","id":1395824,"title":"Past is Prologue Available Now!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-11T06:09:48-07:00","id":1395824,"title":"Past is Prologue Available Now!","content":"Past is Prologue is available now for Dark Ages: Fae!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/317130/Past-is-Prologue?fbclid=IwAR0xiBWDJi-87DiBjBSvCVWEw85wz0IpLWCzaUPOQ9MlxQ1SiXIQtZ5ji6I\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/317130/Past-is-Prologue</a><br /> <br /> Those Who Forget Their History<br /> <br /> The firstborn were not the first beings to emerge from the Mists. The dark \u2014 formless and insubstantial, untainted by Weaving \u2014 were its original inhabitants. Eons ago, the fae fought the dark for the right to determine the nature of the world. The fae won and imprisoned the dark for all eternity.<br /> <br /> Are Doomed to Be Annihilated by It<br /> <br /> Or so they thought. In victory, the fae grew complacent and indulged in their petty grievances. Few fae remain who remember the dark or the Sacred Oaths that lock them away. Now the dark return determined to enact their revenge against the fae.<br /> <br /> Past is Prologue includes:<br /> <br /> \u2022 A new Origin \u2014 the dark, their courts, and their means of reentering the world.<br /> \u2022 A history of the Weaving War and details about the elusive Sacred Oaths.<br /> \u2022 The dark\u2019s fearsome Dominion of Nightmare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T08:15:52-07:00","id":1395845,"title":"","content":"Just bought it. Can\u2019t wait to read it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T12:03:07-07:00","id":1395877,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m super excited and I will purchase it when I get home from work! Charlie you have established yourself as a brand I can trust!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T13:05:15-07:00","id":1395894,"title":"","content":"This book is amazing!!! Are the dark like the Fomorians from C:tD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T14:22:28-07:00","id":1395910,"title":"","content":"It sounds great... I can't wait to read it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T14:50:43-07:00","id":1395917,"title":"","content":"Not bought it yet, but looking forward to it. Seems to be hitting a narrative niche I associated with the Formanians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T07:25:28-07:00","id":1396015,"title":"","content":"Thank you all so much for the kind words!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1395824-past-is-prologue-available-now?p=1395894#post1395894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the dark like the Fomorians from C:tD?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's safe to say the parallels are intentional <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T07:46:17-07:00","id":1396016,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar648_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"648\" data-vbnamecard=\"648\">PookaKnight</a> thank you \ud83d\ude0a, but for real. Is Dark Ages Fae the past of C:tD the way Dark Ages Vampire is for Masquerade? That always confused me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T08:06:27-07:00","id":1396022,"title":"","content":"DA: Fae was written so that it may or may not be. The truth was up to individual Storytellers. At the time it came out, Changeling was one of the least popular World of Darkness games, so DA: Fae intentionally distanced itself from Changeling.<br /> <br /> C20 took the stance that DA: Fae is actually Changeling's historical setting. At the time, I wasn't sure how well it would work out since I remembered the games being so different. When I reread them both to research for my sections of C20, I was pleasantly surprised at how well they lined up with each other. DA: Fae was only missing one notable piece to really be Changeling's back story, but the hints were there in the sidebars. Past is Prologue is intended to provide that missing puzzle piece to truly bridge the gap between the two settings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T08:14:36-07:00","id":1396025,"title":"","content":"Thanks! That makes a lot of sense. And Past is Prologue is literally the best gaming book I ever bought for only $2.99.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T20:57:30-07:00","id":1396599,"title":"","content":"I like it. There are some things that match the direction I was going to go, and some things that I hadn't thought of. I'm impressed at how much light <i>Past is Prologue</i> sheds on the confusing relationship between <i>DA:F </i>and <i>C:TD </i>without making any of it more comprehensible from the changeling point of view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;</span>Explanations exist; they have existed for all time; there is always a well-known solution to every human problem \u2014 neat, plausible, and wrong.<span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;<br /> - H.L. Mencken</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/467-bob-the-skull","name":"Bob the Skull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T08:38:15-07:00","id":1396682,"title":"","content":"I'm so happy you guys enjoy it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T21:20:18-07:00","id":1396802,"title":"","content":"I would say you are teasing us with book making us want more, but really its a solid bit of self contained essentials to widen up Dark Age Fae with this new option. I really dig the Courts, especially their Prisons. And Nightmare is a fine Edition, it is literally the Dominion I wanted, name and all, that I wanted to reveal existed for the Dark Fae of Old to the modern fae.<br /> <br /> Very interesting tie in to the Neverborn, excellent use of the Fomorian Colored Courts. The Green Court is my favorite.<br /> <br /> And the Echoes are solid and seem like the most Evocative of all of Dark Age Fae.<br /> <br /> Many people thought they didn't need this because we already have Winter Court, but damn this showed us a fun twist that Maybe the Witner Court actually weren't the Fomorians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T14:04:10-07:00","id":1398229,"title":"","content":"Congratulations on this amazing book, PookaKnight! I just bought it and I loved it. Only wish it could be a whole big book dedicated to this facet of Fae / Changeling. <br /> <br /> I have to ask: the Dark are the Fomorians, right? How do you see their connection, if any, with the other Big Evils of the World of Darkness? I mean, the Wyrm, but especially the Malfeans from Wraith (which the Green Court feels very related to).<br /> <br /> I'm especially interested in any connection to Demon: the Fallen, if you would have an opinion on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}